{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Young upstarts</b> — little ones, as when they bloom." "<b>They sent forth against my feet</b> — they placed thorns in the path." "<b>And they upheave</b> — from the root סלסל, as in ממאיר."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Hebrew פרחח is a rare/obscure word; rendered hyper-literally as Ibn Ezra's own etymology implies."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:01.655747150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}